      "writtenOn": "2026-05-19T22:49:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can make the loops in `WriteRomData` and `ReadRomData` more concise by using a standard `for` loop with `subspan`.\n\n**Action:** Refactor `WriteRomData` (and apply similar logic to `ReadRomData`):\n\n```c\nint IapControl::WriteRomData(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buff) {\n  if (buff.empty()) return -1;\n\n  for (size_t offset \u003d 0; offset \u003c buff.size(); offset +\u003d kEp3Length) {\n    size_t chunk_size \u003d std::min(kEp3Length, buff.size() - offset);\n    auto chunk \u003d buff.subspan(offset, chunk_size);\n\n    if (IapSendData(chunk)) {\n      LogErr(\"[IAP] {} - fail, count: {}\\n\", __func__, offset);\n      return -1;\n    }\n\n    if (progress_callback_) {\n      progress_callback_(offset + chunk.size(), buff.size());\n    }\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 424,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 478,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "cc2317f413398bf584f742ce8200fe801eec46b5",
