      "writtenOn": "2026-05-19T22:38:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `OpenDevice`:\n\n```c\nif (libusb_kernel_driver_active(dev_handle_ptr_.get(), hid_interfaces_[i])) {\n\n```\n\n`libusb_kernel_driver_active` returns `1` if active, `0` if not, and a *negative* error code if it fails. Because C++ treats any non-zero value as `true`, an error code will mistakenly trigger the detachment logic and log a confusing message.\n\n* **Action:** Explicitly check for `\u003d\u003d 1`:\n\n````c\n    int active \u003d libusb_kernel_driver_active(dev_handle_ptr_.get(), hid_interfaces_[i]);\n    if (active \u003d\u003d 1) {\n        libusb_detach_kernel_driver(...);\n    } else if (active \u003c 0) {\n        LogErr(\"[IAP] {} - Failed to check kernel driver: {}\\n\", __func__, libusb_error_name(active));\n    }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 561,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 561,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "cc2317f413398bf584f742ce8200fe801eec46b5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
